<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Honneur et Patrie, BBC programme</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1943</span><span class="sg-chain-h">whistled signature tune</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Three Songs about Resistance, film (Alberto Cavalcanti)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1943</span><span class="sg-chain-h">first sung in, by Germaine Sablon</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Through Valleys and Over Hills (Russian song)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">by one account, the source of the melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Marche des partisans / Guerilla Song (Anna Marly, Russian words)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1941</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the earlier song with the same tune</span></li></ul></section>
